{%- comment -%}
  Section: siwa-product-row | Owner: A-04 | Task: ST-05

  L-02 ProductGrid, wearing phlur's slot 2 and slot 5. The homepage puts this
  section on the page twice — new drops and best sellers — so nothing in it may
  be true of only one of those two placements. The collection, the heading, the
  card count, the rhythm and the link out are all settings; the section itself
  knows nothing about which row it is.

  EVERY PRODUCT GOES THROUGH snippets/siwa-product-card.liquid.
  Not a copy of it, not a variation on it. The catalog stamp is non-negotiable
  on every thumbnail (CI rule 11) and the only way to guarantee that on two
  homepage rows, a collection page and a search result at once is for all four
  to render the same snippet. That snippet cannot load its own stylesheet, so
  the badge-stack extension it depends on is loaded here, by the caller.

  TWO LAYOUTS, ONE LOOP — deviation D-4.
  Phlur measures a scroll-snap carousel at this slot; DESIGN.md §4 routes any
  set of products to `.siwa-grid`. Both are legitimate, so `layout` carries
  both and defaults to `carousel` for phlur fidelity. The cards are captured
  once and poured into whichever wrapper is asked for — one loop, one card
  contract, two arrangements.

  NO JAVASCRIPT, AND NOT AS A COMPROMISE.
  Phlur's carousel has no scripted controls either: it is `overflow-x: auto`
  plus CSS scroll-snap, which drags with a finger, scrolls with a trackpad and
  is driven from the keyboard by the browser's own scroll handling. A section
  that wrote its own JavaScript would also be a validator error in this theme —
  the behaviour layer is assets/siwa-theme.js and nowhere else.

  A SCROLL CONTAINER IS AN INTERACTIVE CONTROL AND HAS TO BE REACHABLE.
  A `<div>` that scrolls but cannot be focused is unusable by a keyboard, so
  the viewport takes `tabindex="0"`, and because a focusable scroll box needs a
  name it takes `role="region"` and the translated region label with it. The
  track inside is a real `<ul>` so the row announces "list, 12 items" rather
  than twelve loose links (DESIGN.md §3.4). In grid mode nothing scrolls, so
  the region and the tabstop are not rendered at all — an empty tabstop is
  worse than none.

  THE FIRST FOUR CARDS ARE EAGER. The rest are lazy. Four is the number of
  cards that can be inside the first viewport at the widest measured card
  width, so it is a loading budget rather than a piece of content, and it
  stays out of the Customizer for the same reason the breakpoints do.

  THE EMPTY STATE IS A REAL STATE, NOT A GHOST GRID.
  An unset collection, or one whose products are all filtered out by the
  in-stock switch, renders the translated empty line and a way out of it.
  Placeholder cards pretending to be products would be a lie in the one place
  a merchant is most likely to look at a preview and believe it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'siwa-product-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'siwa-product-row.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    The hero owns the h1. This section takes h2 by default and h3 when it sits
    under one, and the cards take the next level down so the outline never
    skips a rank.
  endcomment
  assign heading_tag = s.heading_tag | default: 'h2'
  assign heading_allowed = 'h2,h3' | split: ','
  unless heading_allowed contains heading_tag
    assign heading_tag = 'h2'
  endunless
  assign heading_class = 'siwa-' | append: heading_tag

  assign card_heading = 'h3'
  if heading_tag == 'h3'
    assign card_heading = 'h4'
  endif

  assign row_collection = s.collection

  comment
    14 of the 60 products in this catalogue are fully sold out. Left unfiltered
    a twelve-card row can legitimately fill with cards nobody can buy, so the
    merchant decides — the switch is off by default, because a sold-out card
    still carries a stamp, a name and a price and is honest merchandising.
  endcomment
  assign row_products = row_collection.products
  if s.in_stock_only
    assign row_products = row_products | where: 'available', true
  endif
  assign row_count = row_products.size | default: 0

  assign row_title = s.heading
  if row_title == blank
    assign row_title = row_collection.title
  endif
  assign region_label = 'sections.product_row.region_label' | t: title: row_title

  comment
    The theme's established fallback shape: a blank setting means "use the
    translated default", so a merchant who never opens the field still gets a
    row that reads correctly in Arabic. Same pattern as the footer newsletter.
  endcomment
  assign view_all_label = 'sections.product_row.view_all' | t
  if s.view_all_label != blank
    assign view_all_label = s.view_all_label
  endif

  assign view_all_url = s.view_all_url
  if view_all_url == blank
    assign view_all_url = row_collection.url
  endif

  assign empty_label = 'sections.product_row.empty' | t
  assign empty_action_label = 'sections.product_row.empty_action' | t
  assign empty_url = view_all_url
  if empty_url == blank
    assign empty_url = routes.all_products_collection_url
  endif

  comment
    DESIGN.md §4 alternates commerce and ceremonial rhythm down the page. The
    class carries the rhythm; the padding settings below are ADDED to it, on a
    separate element, so neither silently cancels the other.
  endcomment
  assign rhythm_class = 'siwa-section'
  if s.rhythm == 'tight'
    assign rhythm_class = 'siwa-section--tight'
  endif

  assign is_carousel = false
  if s.layout == 'carousel'
    assign is_carousel = true
  endif
-%}

{% style %}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
    --siwa-row-gap: {{ s.item_gap }}px;
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-product-row__inner {
    padding-block-start: {{ s.padding_top }}px;
    padding-block-end: {{ s.padding_bottom }}px;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Gate 0 finding F2. `.siwa-grid` sets --grid-cols inside max-width queries
    at specificity (0,1,0). A bare `#shopify-section-… { --grid-cols }` rule,
    or an inline style attribute, outranks those at EVERY viewport and freezes
    the desktop column count on a phone. The count is therefore emitted inside
    a min-width query that cannot overlap the collapse — exactly the shape
    sections/siwa-footer.liquid uses for its own column setting.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media (min-width: 1201px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-product-row__grid {
      --grid-cols: {{ s.columns }};
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-product-row__inner {
      padding-block-start: {{ s.mobile_padding_top }}px;
      padding-block-end: {{ s.mobile_padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div class="siwa-product-row__rhythm {{ rhythm_class }}">
  <div class="siwa-container siwa-product-row__inner">
    <div class="siwa-section-heading siwa-product-row__head">
      <div class="siwa-product-row__headings">
        {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="siwa-label siwa-section-heading__eyebrow siwa-product-row__eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
          <{{ heading_tag }} class="{{ heading_class }} siwa-product-row__title">{{ s.heading }}</{{ heading_tag }}>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if s.show_view_all and view_all_url != blank -%}
        <div class="siwa-product-row__action">
          {%- render 'siwa-button', label: view_all_label, href: view_all_url, variant: 'text' -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if row_count > 0 -%}
      {%- capture row_items -%}
        {%- for product in row_products limit: s.product_limit -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign card_lazy = true
            if forloop.index <= 4
              assign card_lazy = false
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="siwa-product-row__item">
            {%- render 'siwa-product-card',
              product: product,
              lazy: card_lazy,
              show_price: s.show_price,
              show_inspired_by: s.show_inspired_by,
              heading_level: card_heading
            -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- if is_carousel -%}
        <div
          class="siwa-product-row__viewport"
          role="region"
          tabindex="0"
          aria-label="{{ region_label | escape }}"
        >
          <ul class="siwa-product-row__track" role="list">{{ row_items }}</ul>
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        <ul class="siwa-grid siwa-product-row__grid" role="list">{{ row_items }}</ul>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- else -%}
      <div class="siwa-empty siwa-product-row__empty">
        <p class="siwa-body siwa-product-row__empty-text">{{ empty_label }}</p>
        {%- render 'siwa-button', label: empty_action_label, href: empty_url, variant: 'secondary' -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product row",
  "class": "siwa-product-row",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Name what is in the row, not the row itself — \"New drops\", \"Best sellers\". Leave blank to show no heading.",
      "default": "New drops"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "info": "A short label above the heading. Optional."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_tag",
      "label": "Heading level",
      "info": "The hero owns the page's only h1. Use h3 only if this row sits underneath another h2.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h2", "label": "h2" },
        { "value": "h3", "label": "h3" }
      ],
      "default": "h2"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "Collection",
      "info": "Homepage-worthy handles in this catalogue: men-new-drops, women-new-drops, men-best-sellers, women-best-sellers, best-sellers, new-drops, for-her, for-him, bundles, original-creations, body-splash."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "product_limit",
      "label": "Products shown",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 16,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 12
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_view_all",
      "label": "Show the link to the whole collection",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "view_all_label",
      "label": "Link label",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated \"Shop all\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "view_all_url",
      "label": "Link URL",
      "info": "Leave blank to link to the collection chosen above."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Card options"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_price",
      "label": "Show prices",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_inspired_by",
      "label": "Show the \"Inspired by\" line",
      "info": "Never shown on a Siwa Original — an Original is inspired by nobody.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "in_stock_only",
      "label": "Hide sold-out products",
      "info": "The catalogue audit found 14 of 60 products fully sold out, so this decides whether the row is allowed to fill with cards nobody can buy. Off keeps them: a sold-out card is still honest merchandising and carries its stamp, name and price.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout & spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "Layout",
      "info": "Carousel is one scrolling row with the next card peeking off the edge. Grid is the design system's product grid, which falls 4 → 3 → 2 on its own.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "carousel", "label": "Carousel" },
        { "value": "grid", "label": "Grid" }
      ],
      "default": "carousel"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns",
      "label": "Columns",
      "info": "Grid layout only, and desktop only. The grid falls to three columns below 1200px and two below 768px on its own.",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "rhythm",
      "label": "Vertical rhythm",
      "info": "A homepage alternates the two. Commerce for product rows, ceremonial for story sections — never two ceremonial blocks in a row.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Commerce" },
        { "value": "section", "label": "Ceremonial" }
      ],
      "default": "tight"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "item_gap",
      "label": "Space between cards",
      "info": "Carousel layout only. The grid takes its gutters from the design system so every grid in the store lines up.",
      "min": 8,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top",
      "info": "Added on top of the vertical rhythm above.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom",
      "info": "Added on top of the vertical rhythm above.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Product row",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "New drops",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "collection": "new-drops",
        "product_limit": 12,
        "show_view_all": true,
        "show_price": true,
        "show_inspired_by": true,
        "in_stock_only": false,
        "layout": "carousel",
        "columns": 4,
        "rhythm": "tight",
        "item_gap": 20
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
